<ResourceGuide>
  <ResourceGuideHero title="What are burn rate and runway?">
    <p class="guide-lead mt-6">Burn rate is how much cash your startup spends each month. Net burn subtracts the cash collected from customers. Runway is how long your available cash will last at that pace: divide available cash by monthly net burn. The result is an estimate, assuming spending and collections stay the same.</p>
    <p class="mt-4">For an early-stage founder, these numbers help answer a practical question: how much time do we have to test our idea, learn from customers, and reach our next milestone? This guide covers pre-revenue and early-revenue teams, with a worked example for a startup operating in Taiwan.</p>
    <nav aria-label="In this guide" class="guide-contents mt-9 guide-small">
      <a href="#gross-vs-net-burn" class="guide-link">Gross vs net burn</a>
      <a href="#calculate-runway" class="guide-link">Calculate runway</a>
      <a href="#runway-example" class="guide-link">Worked example</a>
